window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-9d54fab7ad7294d0"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"compliance-api-and-audit-events\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"compliance-api\">Compliance API 与审计事件</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>如果安全、法律、治理或调查工作流需要可审计记录，请使用 Compliance API。若要衡量产品采用情况和趋势，请使用分析数据，而不是合规记录。</p> <p><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>是当前访问要求、事件覆盖范围、路由、架构、筛选条件、保留期限和请求行为的权威来源。</p> <p>如需了解可用的合规功能及常见集成方式，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Compliance Platform 指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"when-to-use-the-compliance-api\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"compliance-api_1\">何时使用 Compliance API</h2> <p>在以下情况下适合使用 Compliance API：</p> <ul> <li>将受支持的记录导出到审计或调查系统。</li> <li>执行组织的记录保留和法律保全流程。</li> <li>将 Codex 活动与其他安全或身份数据关联起来。</li> <li>支持经批准的安全、法律或治理调查。</li> </ul> <p>它不是生产力仪表盘。不要用它推断代码质量或个人表现。衡量采用情况请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a>或 <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"get-started\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始使用</h2> <ol> <li>打开 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>，确认你的管理员角色可以访问所需的合规资源。</li> <li>持续收集记录时，使用只追加的合规日志流。请在 API 参考中确认当前支持的资源和获取方式。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=download-logs\">下载日志</a>，并在非生产环境的安全信息和事件管理（SIEM）系统或数据湖中测试数据导入。</li> <li>安排持续收集，并对导出的记录应用组织自己的访问、保留和法律保全控制。不要假设来源系统的保留期限可以替代组织的保留政策。</li> </ol> <p>例如，安全团队可以将不可变的合规事件流式传入 SIEM 以供调查，或者将这些事件送入获准使用的电子取证工作流。请以 API 参考为准，获取当前路由和架构；不要从本指南复制端点约定。</p> <p><a id=\"download-logs\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">下载日志</h3> <p>下载 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/downloads/compliance-api/download_compliance_files.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bash 脚本（需联网）</a>或 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/downloads/compliance-api/download_compliance_files.ps1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PowerShell 脚本（需联网）</a>。这两个脚本都会列出并下载指定时间戳之后的所有可用日志文件、处理分页，并将 JSONL 写入标准输出。错误信息会写入标准错误。</p> <p>将 <code>COMPLIANCE_API_KEY</code> 设置为你的 Enterprise Compliance API 密钥。把 <code>&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;</code> 替换为 ChatGPT 工作区 ID 或 API Platform 组织 ID；把 <code>&lt;after&gt;</code> 替换为包含时区的 ISO 8601 时间戳。下面的示例每次获取 100 个 <code>AUTH_LOG</code> 文件。</p> <p>在 macOS 或 Linux 上，先安装 Bash、<code>curl</code> 和 <code>jq</code>，再运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">bash ./download_compliance_files.sh \"&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;\" AUTH_LOG 100 \"&lt;after&gt;\" &gt; output.jsonl\n</code></pre> <p>Windows 脚本支持 PowerShell 5.1 或更高版本。请检查下载的文件。如果 Windows 阻止了该文件，并且组织的执行策略允许解除阻止，可以运行 <code>Unblock-File -Path .\\download_compliance_files.ps1</code>。下面的示例使用 PowerShell 7，以 UTF-8（不带字节顺序标记）的格式保存：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">.\\download_compliance_files.ps1 \"&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;\" AUTH_LOG 100 \"&lt;after&gt;\" |\n  Set-Content -Encoding utf8NoBOM output.jsonl\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"audit-records-for-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work-cloud\">Work Cloud 本地计算机访问的审计记录</h2> <p>Work Cloud 中的本地计算机访问与 Work Cloud 具有相同的 Compliance API 支持。相关记录会出现在 <code>conversation_message</code> 和 <code>codex_log</code> 事件类型下。本地执行还会产生 OpenTelemetry（OTel）事件；配置 OTel 收集器端点即可收集这些事件。请将本地事件与 Compliance API 记录分开收集。这些来源都无法证明每条本地命令、文件操作、屏幕截图、审批或外部操作均已完整记录。</p> <p>设置收集流程时：</p> <ol> <li>对于受支持的 Work 记录，使用 <code>conversation_message</code> 和 <code>codex_log</code>。事件架构、操作标识符和时间戳请查阅 API 参考。</li> <li>确认该工作流的保留和删除行为。</li> <li>执行一个有代表性的任务，并将导出的记录与实际执行的操作进行比对。</li> </ol> <p><strong>策略自动化。</strong>使用策略 API（policy API）管理全局（Global）设置；在 Agent Security（智能体安全）界面管理本地（Local）和 Codex Cloud（Codex 云端）设置。迁移后，原有全局设置 API 工作流仍可使用。请测试脚本和 Terraform 集成，并确认策略分配和排序没有变化。策略自动化应与审计记录获取流程分开检查。策略 API（policy API）的支持范围不会改变 Compliance API 的事件覆盖范围。</p> <p><strong>基于 Hook 的审计。</strong>如果工作区启用了此功能，可使用管理员定义的 MCP Hook（钩子）。它们会在云端协调器（orchestrator）上运行，处理受支持的生命周期事件和工具事件。替换现有审计工作流之前，请测试回调连接、事件覆盖范围和失败时的行为。请将这些记录与 Compliance API 的覆盖范围分开检查。</p> <p><a id=\"confirm-the-administration-boundaries\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">确认管理边界</h2> <p>合规覆盖范围取决于 ChatGPT 工作区及当前 API 参考中列出的产品。Platform API 组织数据遵循其自身的数据和管理控制。</p> <p>当前路由、事件覆盖范围、架构、筛选条件、保留行为、权限要求和请求机制均以 API 参考为准。本页不会重复定义这些约定。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推出指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">治理</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"compliance-api-and-audit-events\">Compliance API and audit events</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use the Compliance API for security, legal, governance, and investigation workflows that require auditable records. Use analytics, not compliance records, to measure adoption and trends.</p> <p>The <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> is the source of truth for current access requirements, event coverage, routes, schemas, filters, retention, and request behavior.</p> <p>For an overview of the available compliance surfaces and common integration patterns, see the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9261474-compliance-api-for-chatgpt-enterprise-edu-and-chatgpt-for-teachers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Compliance Platform guide (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"when-to-use-the-compliance-api\">When to use the Compliance API</h2> <p>The Compliance API is appropriate when you need to:</p> <ul> <li>Export supported records into an audit or investigation system.</li> <li>Apply organizational retention and legal-hold processes.</li> <li>Correlate Codex activity with other security or identity data.</li> <li>Support approved security, legal, or governance investigations.</li> </ul> <p>It's not a productivity dashboard. Don't use it to infer code quality or individual performance. Use <a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a> or the <a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a> for adoption reporting.</p> <h2 id=\"get-started\">Get started</h2> <ol> <li>Open the <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/public/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a> and confirm that your administrator role can access the compliance resources you need.</li> <li>Use the append-only compliance log stream for ongoing collection. Check the API reference for the currently supported resources and retrieval patterns.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=download-logs\">Download log files</a> and test ingestion into a non-production security information and event management (SIEM) system or data lake.</li> <li>Schedule continuous collection and apply your organization's access, retention, and legal-hold controls to exported records. Don't assume the source retention window replaces your organization's retention policy.</li> </ol> <p>For example, a security team can stream immutable compliance events into its SIEM for investigations, or route those events into an approved electronic discovery workflow. Use the API reference for the current routes and schemas rather than copying an endpoint contract from this guide.</p> <h3 id=\"download-logs\">Download logs</h3> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/downloads/compliance-api/download_compliance_files.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bash script (online)</a> or <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/downloads/compliance-api/download_compliance_files.ps1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PowerShell script (online)</a>. Both list and download every available log file after a given timestamp, follow pagination, and write JSONL to standard output. Errors go to standard error.</p> <p>Set <code>COMPLIANCE_API_KEY</code> to your Enterprise Compliance API key. Replace <code>&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;</code> with your ChatGPT workspace ID or API Platform organization ID, and <code>&lt;after&gt;</code> with an ISO 8601 timestamp that includes a time zone. This example retrieves <code>AUTH_LOG</code> files, 100 at a time.</p> <p>On macOS or Linux, install Bash, <code>curl</code>, and <code>jq</code>, then run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">bash ./download_compliance_files.sh \"&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;\" AUTH_LOG 100 \"&lt;after&gt;\" &gt; output.jsonl\n</code></pre> <p>The Windows script supports PowerShell 5.1 or later. Review the downloaded file. If Windows blocks it and your organization's execution policy permits it, run <code>Unblock-File -Path .\\download_compliance_files.ps1</code>. This example uses PowerShell 7 to save UTF-8 without a byte-order mark:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">.\\download_compliance_files.ps1 \"&lt;workspace_or_org_id&gt;\" AUTH_LOG 100 \"&lt;after&gt;\" |\n  Set-Content -Encoding utf8NoBOM output.jsonl\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"audit-records-for-local-computer-access-with-work-cloud\">Audit records for Local computer access with Work Cloud</h2> <p>Local computer access with Work Cloud has the same Compliance API support as Work Cloud. Records appear under the <code>conversation_message</code> and <code>codex_log</code> event types. Local execution also generates OpenTelemetry (OTel) events, which you can collect by configuring an OTel collector endpoint. Collect these local events separately from Compliance API records. These sources do not establish a complete record of every local command, file operation, screenshot, approval, or external action.</p> <p>When setting up collection:</p> <ol> <li> <p>Use <code>conversation_message</code> and <code>codex_log</code> for supported Work records. Use the API reference for their schemas, action identifiers, and timestamps.</p> </li> <li> <p>Confirm retention and deletion behavior for the workflow.</p> </li> <li> <p>Run a representative task and compare the exported records with the actions performed.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Policy automation. Use the policy API to manage Global settings. Manage Local and Codex Cloud settings in the Agent Security UI. Existing Global API workflows remain available after migration. Test scripts and Terraform integrations, and confirm that assignments and policy ordering are unchanged. Review policy automation separately from audit-record retrieval. Policy API support does not change Compliance API event coverage.</p> <p>Hook-based auditing. Where enabled for your workspace, use admin-defined MCP hooks that run on the cloud coordinator (orchestrator) for supported lifecycle and tool events. Before replacing an existing auditing workflow, test the callback connection, event coverage, and failure behavior. Check these records separately from Compliance API coverage.</p> <h2 id=\"confirm-the-administration-boundaries\">Confirm the administration boundaries</h2> <p>Compliance coverage follows the ChatGPT workspace and the products represented in the current API reference. Platform API organization data follows its own API data and administration controls.</p> <p>The API reference owns the current routes, event coverage, schemas, filters, retention behavior, permission requirements, and request mechanics. This page doesn't duplicate that contract.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">Governance</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a></li> </ul>"};
